# Backend Conventions

- Follow existing route/module layout under `backend/`
- Validate inputs at the boundary; return consistent error shapes
- Authn before authz; never trust client-supplied user ids for access control
- Keep business logic out of transport adapters when a service layer exists
- Idempotency for unsafe retries when relevant
- Log with request context; never log secrets or raw tokens
- Prefer explicit status codes and typed response models

See `docs/conventions/backend.md` and `docs/conventions/api.md`
